Tasks can be simply Go structures. Put the tasks as code in the `agent` dir,
plus a simple main.go,
`goto` command should cd to this and compile the agent with ldflags=-s,
then send & run the agent.


Dry-run mode is needed for all tasks.
Allow dry-run-only permission for specific user/machine (like, production).

Start with tasks:
* Template
* Binary
* Service


Do not mimic ansible. Though, equivalents for some functionality would be good
(blockinfile ..etc).


By default work around Linux inconsistencies
(like, service names: ntp/ntpd, ssh/sshd, apache2/httpd
 on ubuntu/centos).

